IMPORT `nii-il06-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-il06-family-on-a-day`

-- Tests for National Insurance Law ss 65-68 (row IL-06). Every expected value was worked out
-- by hand from the SOURCES before the assertion was run, and the working is written beside
-- each group. None was copied from an evaluation. A failing assertion is a finding about the
-- sources or the encoding, never a value to edit.
--
-- Four kinds of expected value appear, and each group says which it is:
--   * [text]: arithmetic or a rule read directly off the Law (source line given);
--   * [nii-basic]: the Institute's table of basic amounts (nii-il06-published-figures.l4);
--   * [nii-rates-YYYY]: the Institute's page of per-child amounts, which prints the amount
--     paid for the first, second, … child, and the s 68(c) supplement. Its heading:
-- ext:[nii-rates-2026] | סכום קצבת הילדים
--       https://www.btl.gov.il/benefits/children/Pages/%d7%a9%d7%99%d7%a2%d7%95%d7%a8%d7%99%20%d7%94%d7%a7%d7%a6%d7%91%d7%94.aspx
--       [nii-rates-2026] fetched directly 2026-10-06 14:08 UTC, sha256 0bf54039e27ec719e1ec190d00e20012d26f88290e9ed2f5a6a4f503c1b4359c
--                        (from 1 January 2026: 173 / 219 / 219 / 219 / 173; supplement 113)
-- ext:[nii-rates-2026] | סכום הקצבה עבור ילדים לפי מיקומם במשפחה (החל מ- 01.01.2026)
--       [nii-rates-2025] Internet Archive capture 20250420005113 (id_ form), sha256 3985123f0d5dfc54d3bd5ef971b23f9ecd59a6f47dd79990ac383ed70b024e64
--                        (from 1 January 2025: 169 / 214 / 214 / 214 / 169; supplement 111)
-- ext:[nii-rates-2025] | סכום הקצבה עבור ילדים לפי מיקומם במשפחה (החל ב- 01.01.2025)
--       [nii-rates-2024] capture 20240806061702, sha256 0c7083ccd45f7eb327c3eda843c83b69f8431a5782262a7a8b6aa0fa798632f6
--                        (from 1 January 2024: 169 / 214 / 214 / 214 / 169; supplement 111)
-- ext:[nii-rates-2024] | סכום הקצבה עבור ילדים לפי מיקומם במשפחה (החל ב- 01.01.2024)
--       [nii-rates-2020] capture 20200821105458, sha256 36b09fd990aec92110dc64e174edca48fbada24bcb895307d13bec84fc65d93c
--                        (children born until 31 May 2003: 152 / 192 / 192 / 340 / 359; supplement 99)
--       [nii-rates-2018] capture 20181003161656, sha256 3a7c5f6f347e48cebd7e199d94d987c0b34419021e4d59c1f1267a81dc5cdb09
--                        (children born until 31 May 2003: 150 / 189 / 189 / 336 / 354; supplement 98)
--     The Institute's figures for s 68(b) and (c) are rounded to whole shekels; this encoding's
--     are before rounding (s 381 is not encoded). Those comparisons assert agreement to within
--     one shekel, and say so.
--   * [fork Fn]: a value that depends on a reading recorded in NOTES.md's fork register.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures — persons`

-- Positional on purpose, under a ruler; each named fixture below says what it is.
--                                          ch 11  housewife resident absent formerly  add.tax  inc.supp maint. >1 woman
GIVEN n IS A STRING
      ch11 IS A BOOLEAN
      housewife IS A BOOLEAN
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
      absent IS A BOOLEAN
      formerly IS A BOOLEAN
      `additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      `income support` IS A BOOLEAN
      maintenance IS A BOOLEAN
      `more than one woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person`
`a person` n ch11 housewife resident absent formerly `additional tax` `income support` maintenance `more than one woman` MEANS
    `A person` WITH
        `name`                                                                                     IS n
        `insured under Chapter 11`                                                                 IS ch11
        `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                                    IS housewife
        `resident in Israel`                                                                       IS resident
        `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`                                IS absent
        `formerly insured`                                                                         IS formerly
        `income chargeable to additional tax under section 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance`      IS `additional tax`
        `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law`                             IS `income support`
        `paid, for the month, a monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law` IS maintenance
        `children by more than one woman`                                                          IS `more than one woman`

-- An insured resident, insured under Chapter 11 (s 65 "insured" (1)).
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`insured` n MEANS `a person` n TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Not insured: neither under Chapter 11 nor resident.
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`not insured` n MEANS `a person` n FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Was insured; on the day, has died or is no longer insured.
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`formerly insured` n MEANS `a person` n FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A resident housewife as defined in s 238, not insured under Chapter 11. She is not insured
-- under either limb of s 65 "insured" on reading (A) of fork F18 (06-HW), which this row takes;
-- on reading (B) she is insured under limb (2). Every test that uses this fixture to make a
-- parent uninsured rests on reading (A), and says so (NOTES.md, fork F18; BACKLOG IL-24).
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`a housewife` n MEANS `a person` n FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`insured, with income chargeable to additional tax,` n MEANS `a person` n TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`insured, paid Income Support,` n MEANS `a person` n TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`insured, paid a maintenance payment,` n MEANS `a person` n TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A person`
`insured, with children by more than one woman,` n MEANS `a person` n TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§§ `Fixtures — parents in a child's record`

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      s IS A `Standing to the child`
      fm IS A `Father or mother`
      w IS A BOOLEAN
      sp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`entry` n s fm w sp MEANS
    `A parent in a child's record` WITH
        `name of the person`             IS n
        `standing`                       IS s
        `father or mother`               IS fm
        `the child is with this person`  IS w
        `support proven`                 IS sp

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`natural father` n w MEANS `entry` n `the child's natural parent` `the child's father` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`natural mother` n w MEANS `entry` n `the child's natural parent` `the child's mother` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`adoptive father` n w MEANS `entry` n `the child's adoptive parent` `the child's father` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`adoptive mother` n w MEANS `entry` n `the child's adoptive parent` `the child's mother` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`step-father` n w MEANS `entry` n `the child's step-parent` `the child's father` w FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`a supporter, support proven,` n w MEANS `entry` n `a person who is not the child's parent` `the child's father` w TRUE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      w IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a child's record`
`a supporter, support not proven,` n w MEANS `entry` n `a person who is not the child's parent` `the child's father` w FALSE

§§ `Fixtures — children and families`

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      dob IS A DATE
      ps IS A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A `A child`
`a child` n dob ps MEANS
    `A child` WITH
        `name`                                          IS n
        `date of birth`                                 IS dob
        `married`                                       IS FALSE
        `absence from Israel`                           IS NOTHING
        `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`  IS FALSE
        `parents`                                       IS ps

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      dob IS A DATE
      ps IS A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A `A child`
`a married child` n dob ps MEANS
    `A child` WITH
        `name`                                          IS n
        `date of birth`                                 IS dob
        `married`                                       IS TRUE
        `absence from Israel`                           IS NOTHING
        `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`  IS FALSE
        `parents`                                       IS ps

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      dob IS A DATE
      ps IS A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
      `left` IS A DATE
      `returned` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `regarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child`
`a child abroad` n dob ps `left` `returned` `regarded` MEANS
    `A child` WITH
        `name`                                          IS n
        `date of birth`                                 IS dob
        `married`                                       IS FALSE
        `absence from Israel`                           IS JUST (`An absence from Israel` WITH `the day the child left Israel` IS `left`, `the day the child returned to Israel` IS `returned`)
        `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`  IS `regarded`
        `parents`                                       IS ps

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      ps IS A LIST OF `A person`
      cs IS A LIST OF `A child`
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`the family on` d `of` ps `and` cs MEANS
    `A family on a day` WITH
        `the day`        IS d
        `the persons`    IS ps
        `the children`   IS cs

-- Avi (the natural father) and Batya (the natural mother); the child is with both.
`Avi and Batya, with both` MEANS LIST (`natural father` "Avi" TRUE), (`natural mother` "Batya" TRUE)

-- Six children, listed out of birth order on purpose (the count is ordered by birth, F4).
`the six children` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Kfir" (YMD 2021 11 30) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2009 1 10)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Ido"  (YMD 2015 9 1)   `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Gil"  (YMD 2011 3 5)   `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Yael" (YMD 2018 2 14)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Hila" (YMD 2013 7 20)  `Avi and Batya, with both`)

`the eldest four` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2009 1 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Gil"  (YMD 2011 3 5)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Hila" (YMD 2013 7 20) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Ido"  (YMD 2015 9 1)  `Avi and Batya, with both`)

`the eldest three` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2009 1 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Gil"  (YMD 2011 3 5)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Hila" (YMD 2013 7 20) `Avi and Batya, with both`)

`the eldest two` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2009 1 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Gil"  (YMD 2011 3 5)  `Avi and Batya, with both`)

-- One child, Noa, born 5 May 2016, with whatever parents a test gives her.
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A `A child`
`Noa, with` ps MEANS `a child` "Noa" (YMD 2016 5 5) ps

`15 June 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 6 15

§§ `Fixtures — reading an answer`

-- These read values out of an answer; they compute no law. Each declines (and so shows as a
-- refused assertion, which check.sh counts as red) if the answer is not the shape expected.
@ref test helper
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`test helper: the facts had a problem` MEANS
    REFUSE "test helper: the facts had a problem"

@ref test helper
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`test helper: there is not exactly one answer for that name` MEANS
    REFUSE "test helper: there is not exactly one answer for that name"

@ref test helper
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`test helper: that person has no allowance` MEANS
    REFUSE "test helper: that person has no allowance"

GIVEN r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`
`the answers in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN LEFT p   THEN `test helper: the facts had a problem`
    WHEN RIGHT as THEN as

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A `The child allowance of a person for the month`
`the answer for` n `in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN a YIELD a's `name of the person` EQUALS n) (`the answers in` r)
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN a's `the answer`
    OTHERWISE `test helper: there is not exactly one answer for that name`

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF `The allowance for a child in the count`
`the lines for` n `in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer for` n `in` r
    WHEN `a monthly child allowance` ls THEN ls
    OTHERWISE `test helper: that person has no allowance`

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the allowances for` n `in` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b), before rounding`) (`the lines for` n `in` r)

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the supplements for` n `in` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the supplement under section 68(c), before rounding`) (`the lines for` n `in` r)

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF `The provision that fixes the allowance for a child`
`the provisions for` n `in` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the provision`) (`the lines for` n `in` r)

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the children counted with` n `in` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `name of the child`) (`the lines for` n `in` r)

GIVEN r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family total in` r MEANS
    `the family's total, before rounding, of` (`the answers in` r)

-- "To within one shekel": the comparison with the Institute's rounded figures.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
x `is within one shekel of` y MEANS
    (x MINUS y) LESS THAN 1 AND (y MINUS x) LESS THAN 1

§§ `The period the text answers`

-- [text + sh-5776-247] s 29(a) of the 5776 Law: ss 1 and 68 in their present wording from 1 May 2015.
#ASSERT `the deposited text of sections 65 to 68 was in force on` (YMD 2015 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the deposited text of sections 65 to 68 was in force on` (YMD 2015 4 30)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the child allowance of each person, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2015 4 30) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest two`) `, at` `the basic amounts printed in paragraph (2)` BECAUSE "this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources"

§§ `The Institute's table of basic amounts`

