§§ `Section 68(c) — the supplement`

-- [text, line 826] 70% of the (2)(c) amount, for the third and the fourth child, where the
-- parent is paid Income Support or a maintenance payment and is entitled for three or more.
-- 2026: 70% × 162 = 113.4. Four children: 173 + 219 + 219 + 219 + 113.4 + 113.4 = 1056.8.
#ASSERT `the supplements for` "Avi" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest four`)) EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 113.4, 113.4
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest four`)) EQUALS 1056.8
-- A maintenance payment instead: the same.
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured, paid a maintenance payment,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest four`)) EQUALS 1056.8
-- Three children: the third only. 173 + 219 + 219 + 113.4 = 724.4.
#ASSERT `the supplements for` "Avi" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest three`)) EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 113.4
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest three`)) EQUALS 724.4
-- Two children: fewer than three, no supplement. 173 + 219 = 392.
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest two`)) EQUALS 392
-- [fork F14] The parent paid Income Support must be the parent in whose count the children are:
-- Batya is paid it, the four are in Avi's count, so no supplement. 173 + 219 × 3 = 830.
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured, paid Income Support,` "Batya") `and` `the eldest four`)) EQUALS 830

-- [nii-rates-2026] supplement 113; [nii-rates-2024], [nii-rates-2025] 111 (70% × 158 = 110.6);
-- [nii-rates-2020] 99 (70% × 142 = 99.4); [nii-rates-2018] 98 (70% × 140 = 98, exact).
#ASSERT (`s 68(c) — the supplement, before rounding, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` `15 June 2026`)) `is within one shekel of` 113
#ASSERT (`s 68(c) — the supplement, before rounding, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (YMD 2025 4 20))) `is within one shekel of` 111
#ASSERT (`s 68(c) — the supplement, before rounding, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (YMD 2024 8 6))) `is within one shekel of` 111
#ASSERT (`s 68(c) — the supplement, before rounding, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (YMD 2020 8 21))) `is within one shekel of` 99
#ASSERT `s 68(c) — the supplement, before rounding, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (YMD 2018 10 3)) EQUALS 98

§§ `Section 68(b) — children born before 1 June 2003, against the Institute's 2018 and 2020 pages`

-- 2018 (day 3 October 2018): five children under 18, the youngest two twins born 10 February
-- 2003. [text] (2)(a) = 150, (2)(b) = 189 in 2018 [nii-basic]: first 150, second 189, third
-- 189, fourth 150 × 2.24 = 336, fifth 150 × 2.36 = 354; total 1218.
-- [nii-rates-2018] children born until 31 May 2003: 150 / 189 / 189 / 336 / 354. Exact.
`the five of 2018` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Dan"   (YMD 2000 11 1) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Eden"  (YMD 2001 9 1)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Gefen" (YMD 2002 6 1)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Hadar" (YMD 2003 2 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Itai"  (YMD 2003 2 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`)

#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2018 10 3) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the five of 2018`)) EQUALS LIST 150, 189, 189, 336, 354
#ASSERT `the provisions for` "Avi" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2018 10 3) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the five of 2018`)) EQUALS LIST `section 68(a), at the basic amount in paragraph (2)(a) of section 1`, `section 68(a), at the basic amount in paragraph (2)(b) of section 1`, `section 68(a), at the basic amount in paragraph (2)(b) of section 1`, `section 68(b)(2), a fourth child born before 1 June 2003`, `section 68(b)(3), a fifth or later child born before 1 June 2003`
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2018 10 3) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the five of 2018`)) EQUALS 1218

-- The same five, but the twins born either side of midnight, 31 May and 1 June 2003: the
-- fourth is under (b)(2), the fifth is NOT born before 1 June 2003 and takes (a) at (2)(a).
-- [text] 150, 189, 189, 336, 150; total 1014.
`the five of 2018, twins either side of 1 June 2003` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Dan"   (YMD 2000 11 1) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Eden"  (YMD 2001 9 1)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Gefen" (YMD 2002 6 1)  `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Hadar" (YMD 2003 5 31) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Itai"  (YMD 2003 6 1)  `Avi and Batya, with both`)

#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2018 10 3) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the five of 2018, twins either side of 1 June 2003`)) EQUALS LIST 150, 189, 189, 336, 150

-- 2020 (day 21 August 2020): quintuplets born 1 March 2003. [nii-basic] (2)(a) = 152, (2)(b)
-- = 192, (2)(c) = 142. [text] 152, 192, 192, 152 × 2.24 = 340.48, 152 × 2.36 = 358.72.
-- With Income Support: supplements 0, 0, 99.4, 99.4, 0.
-- [nii-rates-2020] 152 / 192 / 192 / 340 / 359: the last two agree to within one shekel.
`the quintuplets` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Q1" (YMD 2003 3 1) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Q2" (YMD 2003 3 1) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Q3" (YMD 2003 3 1) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Q4" (YMD 2003 3 1) `Avi and Batya, with both`),
         (`a child` "Q5" (YMD 2003 3 1) `Avi and Batya, with both`)

#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2020 8 21) `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the quintuplets`)) EQUALS LIST 152, 192, 192, 340.48, 358.72
#ASSERT `the supplements for` "Avi" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2020 8 21) `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the quintuplets`)) EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 99.4, 99.4, 0
#ASSERT (`s 68 — the monthly allowance, before rounding, under` `section 68(b)(2), a fourth child born before 1 June 2003` `, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (YMD 2020 8 21))) `is within one shekel of` 340
#ASSERT (`s 68 — the monthly allowance, before rounding, under` `section 68(b)(3), a fifth or later child born before 1 June 2003` `, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (YMD 2020 8 21))) `is within one shekel of` 359
