#ASSERT `the children counted with` "Batya" `in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `not insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` `the eldest two`)) EQUALS LIST "Ella", "Gil"

§§ `Facts that cannot describe a case`

#ASSERT `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Avi") `and` `the eldest two`) EQUALS LEFT `two persons have the same name`
#ASSERT `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi") `and` `the eldest two`) EQUALS LEFT `a child's record names a parent who is not among the persons`
#ASSERT `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` (LIST (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2009 1 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`), (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2011 3 5) `Avi and Batya, with both`))) EQUALS LEFT `two children have the same name`
#ASSERT `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` (LIST (`a child` "Noa" (YMD 2026 6 16) `Avi and Batya, with both`))) EQUALS LEFT `a child is born after the day`
#ASSERT `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` `15 June 2026` `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` (LIST (`a child abroad` "Noa" (YMD 2016 5 5) `Avi and Batya, with both` (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING FALSE))) EQUALS LEFT `an absence from Israel begins after the day, or ends before it begins`

-- Version 0.2.0 (06-F5; INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md, finding 5). [text, line 807; the noun's contract]
-- Noa left on 10 January 2026 and came back on 10 June 2026. Asked about 1 September 2026, the
-- absence is over: it is not "the absence in progress on the day", so the facts are reported,
-- not read (before 0.2.0 Noa was treated as abroad and the family's total was 0). The same on
-- 11 June, the day after her return.
#ASSERT `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2026 9 1) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` (LIST (`a child abroad` "Noa" (YMD 2016 5 5) `Avi and Batya, with both` (YMD 2026 1 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) FALSE))) EQUALS LEFT `an absence from Israel ended before the day`
#ASSERT `the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2026 6 11) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` (LIST (`a child abroad` "Noa" (YMD 2016 5 5) `Avi and Batya, with both` (YMD 2026 1 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) FALSE))) EQUALS LEFT `an absence from Israel ended before the day`
-- [fork F3, the return day; assumed, not ruled] On 10 June itself the absence is in progress, as
-- this row has always read it: it ran from 10 January to 10 June, more than three months (which end
-- on 10 April), so Noa is abroad on that day and in no count. Total 0, not a problem with the facts.
#ASSERT NOT `s 65 — in Israel on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `:` (`a child abroad` "Noa" (YMD 2016 5 5) `Avi and Batya, with both` (YMD 2026 1 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `of` (LIST `insured` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` (LIST (`a child abroad` "Noa" (YMD 2016 5 5) `Avi and Batya, with both` (YMD 2026 1 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) FALSE)))) EQUALS 0

§§ `A family in a month — the children section 72 pays for (version 0.2.0, 06-S72)`

-- [text, s 72(a), line 854, with s 65's proviso, line 807] s 72(a) pays the allowance to the last
-- day of the month in which entitlement ceased, and from the 1st of the month in which it arose
-- if it arose by the 15th. The caller (row IL-08 encodes s 72) lists the children it pays for in
-- the month; this row counts them for that month. Amounts [nii-basic] for 2026: (2)(a) 173,
-- (2)(b) 219, (2)(c) 162; the s 68(c) supplement 70% × 162 = 113.4.

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      ps IS A LIST OF `A person`
      cs IS A LIST OF `A child`
GIVETH A `A family in a month`
`the family in the month of` d `of` ps `, paid for:` cs MEANS
    `A family in a month` WITH
        `a day in the month, on which the facts stand`   IS d
        `the persons`                                    IS ps
        `the children section 72 pays for in the month`  IS cs

GIVEN f IS A `A family in a month`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` f MEANS
    `the child allowance of each person for the month, for the children section 72 pays for, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the month, in` f

`Avi and Batya, insured` MEANS LIST (`insured` "Avi"), (`insured` "Batya")

-- Keren turns 18 on 1 November 2026.
`Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026` MEANS `a child` "Keren" (YMD 2008 11 1)  `Avi and Batya, with both`
`Gil, born 5 March 2011`       MEANS `a child` "Gil"   (YMD 2011 3 5)   `Avi and Batya, with both`
`Hila, born 20 July 2013`      MEANS `a child` "Hila"  (YMD 2013 7 20)  `Avi and Batya, with both`
`Ido, born 1 September 2015`   MEANS `a child` "Ido"   (YMD 2015 9 1)   `Avi and Batya, with both`

-- Keren alone, November 2026. Her entitlement ceased on 1 November, in November, so s 72(a) pays
-- November. She is with both parents, so in Avi's count (first limb), the first child: 173.
#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`))) EQUALS LIST 173
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`))) EQUALS 173
-- Any day of November names the same month: as at 30 November, 173.
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 30) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`))) EQUALS 173
-- The day question about 1 November still excludes her, for she is 18 on that day: 0. That is the
-- right answer for the day, and the reason the month question exists.
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `and` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`))) EQUALS 0

-- [fork F19] Keren with Gil and Hila, November 2026: the count for the month is the three, eldest
-- first: Keren 173, Gil 219, Hila 219; total 611. The day question about 1 November counts two:
-- Gil 173, Hila 219; total 392.
#ASSERT `the children counted with` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`))) EQUALS LIST "Keren", "Gil", "Hila"
#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`))) EQUALS LIST 173, 219, 219
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`))) EQUALS 611
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `and` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`))) EQUALS 392
-- December 2026: s 72 no longer pays for Keren; the caller lists Gil and Hila: 173 + 219 = 392.
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 12 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`))) EQUALS 392
-- Listing Keren for December contradicts s 72(a): her entitlement ceased in November.
#ASSERT `the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 12 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`)) EQUALS LEFT `a child said to be paid for in the month reached 18 before the month began`

-- [fork F19; text, line 826] s 68(c) on the month's count. Avi is paid Income Support; Keren, Gil,
-- Hila and Ido, November 2026. Four children: 173 + 219 × 3 = 830; the supplement for the third
-- (Hila) and the fourth (Ido), 113.4 each; total 830 + 226.8 = 1056.8. The day question about
-- 1 November counts three (Gil 173, Hila 219, Ido 219) and adds the supplement for the third (Ido)
-- only: 611 + 113.4 = 724.4.
#ASSERT `the supplements for` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`, `Ido, born 1 September 2015`))) EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 113.4, 113.4
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`, `Ido, born 1 September 2015`))) EQUALS 1056.8
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` (LIST `insured, paid Income Support,` "Avi", `insured` "Batya") `and` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`, `Ido, born 1 September 2015`))) EQUALS 724.4

-- A birth by the 15th: Gal, born 10 September 2026; s 72(a) pays September. With Ella (born 10
-- January 2009) and Gil, asked as at 1 September, before the birth: 173, 219, 219; total 611.
#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 9 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2009 1 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`), `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, (`a child` "Gal" (YMD 2026 9 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`)))) EQUALS LIST 173, 219, 219
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 9 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST (`a child` "Ella" (YMD 2009 1 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`), `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, (`a child` "Gal" (YMD 2026 9 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`)))) EQUALS 611
-- A child listed for September but born on 2 October: s 72 cannot pay a month before the birth.
#ASSERT `the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 9 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, (`a child` "Gal" (YMD 2026 10 2) `Avi and Batya, with both`))) EQUALS LEFT `a child said to be paid for in the month is born after the month`

-- [fork F19] An 18th birthday and a birth in one month: Tal turns 18 on 10 September 2026 and Gal
-- is born on 12 September 2026, with Gil and Hila. No day of September finds Tal under 18 and Gal
-- born; s 72(a) pays both for the month. Eldest first: Tal 173, Gil 219, Hila 219, Gal 219; total 830.
`Tal, Gil, Hila and Gal` MEANS
    LIST (`a child` "Tal" (YMD 2008 9 10) `Avi and Batya, with both`), `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`, (`a child` "Gal" (YMD 2026 9 12) `Avi and Batya, with both`)
#ASSERT `the children counted with` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 9 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `Tal, Gil, Hila and Gal`)) EQUALS LIST "Tal", "Gil", "Hila", "Gal"
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 9 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `Tal, Gil, Hila and Gal`)) EQUALS 830
#ASSERT `s 67(a) — no child is counted with more than one insured parent, for the month, in` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 9 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `Tal, Gil, Hila and Gal`)

-- Where every child listed is born and under 18 on the record's day, the month question gives the
-- day question's answer: the six children, June 2026, 173, 219, 219, 219, 173, 173, total 1176
-- (as asserted above for 15 June [nii-rates-2026]), whether asked as at 15 June or 1 June.
#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` `15 June 2026` `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `the six children`)) EQUALS LIST 173, 219, 219, 219, 173, 173
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `the six children`)) EQUALS 1176

-- [fork F2, reading (i), clamp; DATE in BACKLOG IL-24] Born 29 February 2008: 18 on 28 February
-- 2026. February 2026 is paid on every reading (the birthday falls in it or on 1 March): 173. For
-- March, on reading (i) her entitlement ceased in February, so a list that names her is a problem
-- with the facts; on reading (ii), 18 on 1 March, s 72 would pay March.
#ASSERT `the family total in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 2 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST (`a child` "Noa" (YMD 2008 2 29) `Avi and Batya, with both`)))) EQUALS 173
#ASSERT `the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST (`a child` "Noa" (YMD 2008 2 29) `Avi and Batya, with both`))) EQUALS LEFT `a child said to be paid for in the month reached 18 before the month began`

-- [text + sh-5776-247; nii-basic] The period: April 2015 is declined; May 2015 is answered at the
-- 2015 amounts (two children, 150 and 188), asked as at 20 May; January 2027 has no published figures.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2015 4 30) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `the eldest two`) BECAUSE "this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources"
#ASSERT `the allowances for` "Avi" `in` (`the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2015 5 20) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `the eldest two`)) EQUALS LIST 150, 188
#ASSERT REFUSED `the month's answer, at the Institute's amounts, for` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2027 1 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` `the eldest two`) BECAUSE "the basic amounts for the child allowance from 1 January 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched"

-- The age limb for a month, by itself: Keren in November (18 on its 1st) and not in December; Gal,
-- born 12 September 2026, in September and not in August.
#ASSERT `s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` (YMD 2026 11 15) `began, and born by its end:` `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` (YMD 2026 12 1) `began, and born by its end:` `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`
#ASSERT `s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` (YMD 2026 9 1) `began, and born by its end:` (`a child` "Gal" (YMD 2026 9 12) `Avi and Batya, with both`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` (YMD 2026 8 31) `began, and born by its end:` (`a child` "Gal" (YMD 2026 9 12) `Avi and Batya, with both`)

-- The month's forms beside the day's, in nii-s65-interpretation.l4, nii-s67-count-of-children.l4
-- and nii-s68-amount.l4 (the entry points a caller such as the capstone may use one by one).
-- Keren, Gil and Hila, November 2026, as at 1 November: Keren is a child for the month (her 18th
-- birthday is its 1st) and not on that day; she is in Avi's count (first limb, with both); Avi's
-- count for the month is the three, eldest first; Batya, insured, has an allowance with no lines.
#ASSERT `s 65 — a child for this Chapter, for the month section 72 pays, in` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`)) `:` `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 65 — a child for this Chapter, in` (`the family on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `and` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`)) `:` `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`
#ASSERT `s 67 — the insured parent in whose count, for the month, in` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`)) `, is` `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026` EQUALS JUST "Avi"
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `name`) (`s 67 — the count of children, for the month, in` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`)) `, of` (`insured` "Avi")) EQUALS LIST "Keren", "Gil", "Hila"
#ASSERT `s 68 — the child allowance for the month, in` (`the family in the month of` (YMD 2026 11 1) `of` `Avi and Batya, insured` `, paid for:` (LIST `Keren, 18 on 1 November 2026`, `Gil, born 5 March 2011`, `Hila, born 20 July 2013`)) `, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (YMD 2026 11 1)) `, of` (`insured` "Batya") EQUALS `a monthly child allowance` EMPTY
